{#
    A labelled control with its rule in prose and its violations hung off it. `forms/Field`.

    Parameters:
      label       the control's name, in the interface's voice
      name        the form field name, used for `id` and for the violations' propertyPath
      hint        optional, the rule as a sentence. Prose, never a regex, and written from the
                  same domain constants the constraint cites so the two cannot drift
      value       optional, what to put back in the control
      violations  optional, a list of {message, code} already filtered to this field's
                  propertyPath
      type        optional, defaults to `text`

    The `control` block is what a select or a textarea overrides, which means `{% embed %}` and
    not `{% include %}`; an include cannot override a block.

    THE RULE THIS PARTIAL CARRIES, and the reason it is foundation rather than one card's work:
    a 422 with a list of violations and a 409 with one problem document render identically here.
    Both arrive carrying a `propertyPath`, so the page uses it even when the failure came back
    alone. Two exception branches in the controller, one visual result on the page. Option A
    emits Symfony's constraint UUIDs and option B the declared codes; this template cannot tell
    them apart and must not try.

    The field keeps what was typed, including on a conflict. A form that clears itself punishes
    the reader for the server's opinion.

    The code renders quietly, in mono and `--ink-faint`, because it is what a reader quotes in a
    bug report and what the RFC 9457 type is built from. It is never the loudest thing in the
    message.

    A query-parameter parse failure has no field to sit under, so it never comes here: ADR 004's
    400 is a `_notice.html.twig` above the list, and the list still renders with the filters that
    did parse.
#}
{% set violations = violations|default([]) %}
<label class="field{{ violations is not empty ? ' field--invalid' : '' }}" for="{{ name }}">
    <span class="field__label label">{{ label }}</span>
    {% block control %}
        <input class="input"
               type="{{ type|default('text') }}"
               id="{{ name }}"
               name="{{ name }}"
               value="{{ value|default('') }}"
               {% if violations is not empty %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{% for violation in violations %}{{ name }}-violation-{{ loop.index }}{{ loop.last ? '' : ' ' }}{% endfor %}"{% endif %}>
    {% endblock %}
    {% if hint is defined and hint is not empty %}
        <span class="field__hint body-sm">{{ hint }}</span>
    {% endif %}
    {% for violation in violations %}
        <span class="violation body-sm" id="{{ name }}-violation-{{ loop.index }}">
            <span>{{ violation.message }}</span>
            <span class="violation__code code">{{ violation.code }}</span>
        </span>
    {% endfor %}
</label>
